Quotidian bundles material that is not covered by its MIT licence. As an SPDX
expression the repository as a whole is:

    MIT AND OFL-1.1 AND CC-BY-SA-4.0


Fonts — SIL Open Font License 1.1
---------------------------------
firmware/src/fonts/font_*.h

Generated by firmware/tools/fontconvert.py from Cabin (Pablo Impallari,
Rodrigo Fuenzalida, Dave Crossland). They hold Cabin's rasterised outlines and
are therefore a derivative of the font, so the OFL applies to them rather than
the MIT licence covering the code.

    Licence: firmware/src/fonts/OFL.txt
    Upstream: https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Cabin

The OFL permits this bundling. It requires that the notice travels with the
font data, which is what this file and OFL.txt are for.


Quotations — CC BY-SA 4.0
-------------------------
data/

Quotations and biographical dates from Wikiquote and Wikidata.

    Licence: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Every entry in data/quotes-by-day.json records its own license, licenseUrl,
sourceUrl and attributionRequired flag. The flag is true for all 41363 entries,
and the display renders the credit line accordingly - see drawFooter() in
firmware/src/main.cpp. Anything reusing this data must keep that attribution
and share adaptations under the same terms.
